# The Incus layer of the shared OCI system images that the Trove guest image
# derives from, by digest: ghcr.io/fivetime/oci-system/incus, flavor
# ubuntu_noble, fuse4fs in place of fuse2fs (the Incus driver's
# hw_incus_data_volume_fuse=fuse4fs) from fivetime/e2fsprogs 4461e1b1: an
# owner reaches its own files; the fuse4fs that Incus starts for a fuseblk
# mount (an intercepted mount on a Flavor with
# incus:intercept_data_volume_mounts) takes -o kernel,noexcl, so umount
# returns only after fuse4fs has written everything back; and resize2fs
# run as root in the guest grows the mounted filesystem online
# (EXT4_IOC_RESIZE_FS, which the Incus fork intercepts). Move it when
# openstack-cloud-images publishes a newer Incus layer and the Incus
# driver's gate has passed on it.
BASE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/fivetime/oci-system/incus@sha256:a89c9a70bcb5fdbddeea96f7307e2db25981a0ea3e4214d6828043f44b6e4465
